# Working files that should not be served from emr-inc.net.

# CORRECTED, 2026-10-08. The 2026-09-29 note that stood here said the apex was
# GitHub Pages and that nothing could be withheld from emr-inc.net by listing it
# in this file. The first half is wrong, so the second half was too. Measured:
#
#   emr-inc.net        -> 216.150.1.1, 216.150.16.193   Vercel
#   www.emr-inc.net    -> 216.150.1.1, 216.150.1.129    Vercel
#   emr-inc.github.io  -> 2606:50c0:800x::153           GitHub Pages, a DIFFERENT host
#
# and the Vercel project `emr-inc-site` holds both `emr-inc.net` and
# `www.emr-inc.net` as project domains. So VERCEL SERVES THE APEX, this file does
# govern what emr-inc.net serves, and an entry here does withhold a file from it.
#
# ⚠️ BUT THE OLD NOTE'S ADVICE STILL HOLDS, FOR A DIFFERENT REASON. An entry here
# is not how you unpublish anything, because:
#   1. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Every committed file is world-readable on
#      github.com whatever Vercel serves, and stays in the history after a delete.
#   2. GitHub Pages is ALSO enabled on this repo and builds every push to `main`
#      independently of Vercel. It is not in the apex's serving path, but it is a
#      second published copy of the branch root.
# So: withholding a file from the public still means keeping it out of the branch,
# and removing one already committed still means a history purge. That is what the
# dispatch capture needed on 2026-09-29, and why the entry tried first "looked
# like it had worked and had not" — it had worked, for Vercel, and the file was
# still readable by the two routes above.
#
# Pages being enabled and pointed at a custom domain whose DNS goes to Vercel is
# its own loose end: worth deciding whether Pages should be switched off at all,
# rather than left building a parallel copy nobody reads.

DESIGN-BRIEF.md
MIGRATION.md
build-standalone.py
*-standalone.html
experiments/
dns/
